.th SACOPY VIII 12/17/75
.sh NAME
sacopy \*- stand-alone disk copier and compactor (rk05's)
.sh SYNOPSIS
@_/usr/mdec/sacopy
.br
your command line <return>
.sh DESCRIPTION
\fISacopy\fR is a stand-alone disk copier and compactor for rk11 disks.
Program produced output in the synopsis is underlined.
The command line has the following syntax:
.s3
	\fIfrom\fR x \fIto\fR y \fIinoff\fR x1 \fIoutoff\fR options
.s2
.lp +16 8
\fIoption	meaning\fR
.s1
.lp +16 8
copy	Copy from disk \fIx\fR (default 0) to disk \fIy\fR (default 1).
Map physical blocks
on input by adding \fIx1\fR modulo 4872 (default 2400), and on output by adding \fIy1\fR modulo 4872 (default 2400).
The values x1 and y1 allow conversion to and from special format shuffled disks - on non-Princeton
disks, they should be specified as 0!
.lp +16 8
fast	A fast copy omits the unix file structure compactification.
.lp +16 8
verify	Verify the copy. May only be specified with \fIfast\fR.
.lp +16 8
format	Format the output disk before the copy commences.
.lp +16 8
quit	Return control to the bootstrap when copy is complete.
.s3
.i0
Non-Princeton users may want to adjust the additive offset defaults,
and the maximum number of inodes.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
dcopy(VIII)
